  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nSteps 11 and 12 of [potentially reset the focus given a NavigateEvent *event*](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#potentially-reset-the-focus) are currently\n\n> 11. If focusTarget is null, then set focusTarget to document's [document element](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#document-element).\n> 12. Run the [focusing steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#focusing-steps) for focusTarget, with document's [viewport](https://drafts.csswg.org/css2/#viewport) as the fallback target.\n\nHowever it is possible for the document element to be null, and the focusing steps don't accept null.\nPerhaps step 11 can say instead \"set focusTarget to document's viewport\"? (I think it would have essentially the same effect, since getting the focusable area for the document element returns the viewport anyways)\n\nRelated Gecko bug: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2040190",
